<title>JAPAN: Fujitsu says it, Alcatel in supply talks with BT.</title>
<headline>Fujitsu says it, Alcatel in supply talks with BT.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Fujitsu Ltd said on Monday that it and France's Alcatel are in talks with British Telecommunications Plc on supplying BT with transmission equipment to upgrade subscriber phone lines.</p>
<p>&quot;We are in such talks with BT,&quot; a Fujitsu spokesman said. &quot;But nothing has been decided yet.&quot;</p>
<p>BT plans to upgrade subscriber lines connecting telephone exchanges and homes so they can carry more information than the current copper voice lines, he said.</p>
<p>He said he had no other details of the talks or the BT project.</p>
</text>
